From 8db15ae2527c91c899356e06140d33f8c15b22a7 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Rasheed <99349713+gitRasheed@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sat, 31 Oct 2026 23:37:07 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 18/61] NNS.ARMA: honour negative.values in the nonlinear
 estimates

The per-lag nonlinear estimates were always clipped with pmax(0, .),
while the linear branch is guarded by if(!negative.values). Every nonlin
(and the nonlin half of "both") forecast of returns, spreads or demeaned
data was floored at 0, even with negative.values = TRUE or when negative
values were auto-detected from the series.

Before -> after: 3*sin(2*pi*t/12) + N(0, 0.5^2), t = 1..240 (seed 1),
NNS.ARMA(s, h = 12, seasonal.factor = 12, negative.values = TRUE):
  1.63 2.76 2.46 1.01 1.16 0.34  0      0      0      0      0     0.02
  1.63 2.76 2.46 1.01 1.16 0.34 -1.52 -2.66 -2.67 -3.26 -0.91  0.02
  (true signal for months 7..11: -1.5 -2.6 -3.0 -2.6 -1.5)

Series that stay non-negative (negative.values = FALSE) are unchanged
(AirPassengers nonlin/lin/both identical).
---
 R/ARMA.R | 2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/R/ARMA.R b/R/ARMA.R
index 8ee1b15..7779bec 100644
--- a/R/ARMA.R
+++ b/R/ARMA.R
@@ -243,7 +243,7 @@ NNS.ARMA <- function(variable,
           last.y + (rise / run)
         })
         
-        Regression.Estimates <- pmax(0, Regression.Estimates)
+        if(!negative.values) Regression.Estimates <- pmax(0, Regression.Estimates)
         Nonlin.estimates <- sum(Regression.Estimates * Weights)
       }
       
